Checking the codebase against the plan to identify gaps that warrant dynamic archetypes.
{"archetypes":[{"name":"bootstrap-envelope-wiring","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan expands ROUTING_KEYS, adds PHANTOM_* stdout-only advisory tails, and introduces DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED plus synthesized REBASE_RC while keeping invoke rc 0 on rebase conflict; static reviewers rarely trace every consumer of _filtered_envelope, parse_routing_main, and bootstrap-routing.env together.","prompt_body":"Audit whether the planned new routing keys (DEGRADED, BOTH_DOWN, DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED, ROUTE, REBASE_RC, REBASE_OUTCOME, CONFLICT_FILES, REBASE_ERROR, SKIPPED_ALREADY_PUSHED, SKIPPED_ALREADY_FRESH) are wired consistently through python/bootstrap.py ROUTING_KEYS, _filtered_envelope, _shell_assignments, invoke_main stdout, and bootstrap-routing.env writes. Verify PHANTOM_* lines stay off ROUTING_KEYS and off the env file while still appearing on stdout. Check that DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true legitimately leaves ROUTE absent without being treated as rebase failure, and that conflict/bail paths emit ROUTE plus REBASE_RC while bootstrap invoke still exits 0 so the orchestrator branches from envelope KVs not wrapper failure. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"degraded-gate-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Absorbing the degraded gate into Python must mirror skills/design/scripts/design-step0-degraded.sh and skills/shared/external-reviewers.md BOTH_DOWN fail-closed semantics; a subtle drift in non-interactive detection, explanation relay, or sentinel handling would re-prompt or skip 1.r incorrectly.","prompt_body":"Compare the planned bootstrap continue-tail degraded gate against the shipped design-step0-degraded.sh reference and external-reviewers.md contract. Verify BOTH_DOWN uses exact-string false for one-down auto-proceed and treats missing or malformed BOTH_DOWN as prompt-required interactively but contract-failure non-interactively. Confirm the full DEGRADED_EXPLANATION block relays to operator-visible stderr without polluting parseable stdout, the IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR sentinel suppresses re-prompt on resume, non-interactive runs never emit DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED, and 1.r is skipped whenever DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED is true. Check that step-0-bootstrap.sh forwards an explicit non-interactive signal rather than relying on LARCH_SKILL_NON_INTERACTIVE alone. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"orchestrator-macro-sync","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Step 1.r moves inside bootstrap but skills/implement/SKILL.md Rebase Checkpoint Macro still mandates parsing probe process rc and standalone foreground probes; the plan must reconcile anti-halt routing, macro prose, and rebase-checkpoint-routing.md load rules for envelope-only 1.r outcomes.","prompt_body":"Trace how absorbed Step 1.r results reach the orchestrator after removing the standalone degraded-gate and 1.r Bash fences. Check whether skills/implement/SKILL.md routing table, anti-halt continuation text, and the Rebase Checkpoint Macro section still instruct parsing a probe process rc or launching a foreground 1.r probe when bootstrap already synthesized REBASE_RC and ROUTE on rc 0. Verify rebase-checkpoint-routing.md early-note rules align with DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED suppressing missing-ROUTE rebase failure and with loading the reference only on ROUTE conflict, bail, or malformed route after a continue-tail attempt. Flag any leftover Step 0 prose that routes through standalone 1.r or treats bootstrap wrapper rc as rebase failure. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
